================================================================================
                              EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
================================================================================

The 3D Design Club of William Lyon Mackenzie Collegiate Institute proposes to 
organize and execute the "Mackenzie Design Cup 2026" (MDC 2026), a multi-school 
3D design competition hosted at a post-secondary educational institution.

This proposal requests formal administration approval to:
  • Organize a student-led 3D design competition representing our school
  • Host the event at an external post-secondary venue
  • Invite student participants from schools across the Greater Toronto Area
  • Represent William Lyon Mackenzie CI in a public, external educational event

The event is planned for September 2026 and will feature student-created 3D 
designs, professional mentorship sessions, and award recognition. External 
sponsorship commitments are currently being finalized.

================================================================================
                          1. EVENT OVERVIEW & OBJECTIVES
================================================================================

EVENT NAME:              Mackenzie Design Cup 2026
EVENT TYPE:              Student-Led 3D Design Competition
THEME:                   "Design the Future"
PROPOSED DATE:           September 2026 [Specific dates TBD]
EXPECTED DURATION:       Full Day
ORGANIZER:               Rudra Garg (3D Design Club)
TEACHER SUPERVISOR:      Mr. Andrew Archer

COMPETITION FORMAT:
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ✓ Students create 3D designs representing:
    - Future technology concepts
    - Innovative city designs
    - Cutting-edge inventions
  
  ✓ Participants engage in:
    - Professional workshops conducted by industry experts
    - Mentorship sessions with design professionals
    - Peer collaboration and networking
  
  ✓ Event culminates in:
    - Final project submission and judging
    - Awards ceremony recognizing top designs
    - Recognition of participating schools

TARGET PARTICIPANTS:
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  • Primary: Students from William Lyon Mackenzie CI
  • Secondary: Students from schools across the Greater Toronto Area
  • Grade levels: 9 - 12
  • Expected participation: 50+ students from across the TDSB

